  },
  {
    "insert": "The exposé should focus on a few specific, well-defined research questions, and describe experiments that tackle these questions in great detail. Although the goal of the exposé is stated in the motivation, it is not formalized in the form of research questions. In consequence, the scope and focus of the exposé remain unclear"
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "indent": 2,
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "Informal language:",
    "attributes": {
      "bold": true
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet",
      "indent": 1
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": " A scientific exposé should be written in formal, professional language. This exposé uses a quite informal tone and is written in first-person.  Sentences like „I will use my personal DSLR camera“ challenge the scientific credibility of the work. Using formal expressions like „We will use a DSLR camera…“ would improve the tone of this exposé."
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "indent": 2,
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\nOverall, this exposé covers a very interesting and cool research idea. By giving it a stronger research focus, it could be improved even more. I am looking forward to the final version!"
